"""Render the review document from the single spec and measured fit report."""
import json

def compact(x):return json.dumps(x,ensure_ascii=False,separators=(',',':'))
def cell(x):return str(x).replace('|','\\|').replace('\n',' ')
def write_report(s,w,m,root):
 p=[]
 def line(x=''):p.append(x)
 def table(headers,rows):
  line('| '+' | '.join(headers)+' |');line('| '+' | '.join('---' for _ in headers)+' |')
  for r in rows:line('| '+' | '.join(cell(x) for x in r)+' |')
  line()
 def title(x):line('## '+x);line()
 line('# Aero Playground island world — Phase 1A.2');line()
 line('**G1a — PENDING Ty. Design, documentation and review generators only. No Phase 1B work or runtime approval.**');line()
 line('The 19 original grade failures and seven spacing conflicts have been addressed. Full water surfaces are included, so a cut lake bed cannot hide an obstruction above it. Every supplied final is checked across its whole protection fan; every known airway and proposed perimeter segment is checked across its full 2 nm terrain swath. Remaining failures and missing procedure geometry are explicit below. No failed check is converted into an approved waiver.');line()
 title('Authority, frame and numerical status')
 line('Ty’s original Phase 1A brief and nine decisions dated 2026-10-30 govern. The Cursor source Page remains inaccessible; the complete brief restatement is the source of truth. The baseline is local commit `048d9cd`. No new branch, push, merge, rebase, deployment, game-code edit or other-worktree edit belongs to this package.');line()
 line('Coordinates are km east/north from Frank Church summit (0,0); true north is up. Engine mapping remains `(simX,simY,simZ)=(1000*north,1000*east,-0.3048*MSL_ft)`. Physics headings are true; published magnetic courses are true minus the locked 7° E. Supplied ICAO field elevations, runway lengths, Lake Powell 3,700 ft, glacier landing zones 1,000–1,300 ft, Drake’s 4,700 ft valley and 2,992 ft strip, pirate cave dimensions, Catalina position and the 20 km ring are retained.');line()
 line('Main coast extent is **'+str(w['main_island_size_km_computed'])+' km**, versus approximately 18.3 × 17.5 km in the locked context. This western expansion is explicitly **TY1, pending**, not silently approved. Five outer runway islands and the combat islets remain inside the same 20 km ring.');line()
 line('Every authored number is a **design target** unless Ty explicitly locked it. Fit-report numbers are **computed measurements/proofs**, with their stated representation limits. A 100 m review bake is not an engine-ready terrain import or flight certification.');line()
 title('Fit check — baseline to revision')
 table(['Rule','1A result','1A.2 result','Computed evidence'],[(r['rule'],s['baseline_1a']['fit_check'][r['rule']-1]['status'],r['status'],r['evidence']) for r in m['fit_check']])
 line('Full machine-readable evidence, active MOA polygon unions, exclusion masks, raised-floor masks, cave proofs and individual field results: [island-fit-check.json](island-fit-check.json).');line()
 line('Flat-field pairs checked: **'+str(m['flat_pairs_checked'])+'**. Maximum edge-to-edge mean grade: **'+str(m['maximum_grade']['grade_percent'])+'%**, '+', '.join(m['maximum_grade']['fields'])+'. All padded rectangles, including outer runways, six beaches and AP8’s float lane, are included. The 35% cap applies between flat fields, not peaks/canyon walls or explicitly sloped strips.');line()
 title('Remaining approach failures and unresolved geometry')
 table(['Final/end','Terrain penetration m','Pad / water penetration m','Limiting pad'],[(a['title'],a['maximum_m'],str(a['pad_overlay_penetration_m'])+' / '+str(a['water_surface_penetration_m']),a.get('pad')) for a in m['approach_failures']])
 if not m['approach_failures']:line('No known terrain/pad penetration remains.');line()
 table(['Final','Obstacle','Penetration/bound m'],[(a['final'],a['obstacle'],a.get('penetration_m',a.get('conservative_penetration_bound_m'))) for a in m['approach_obstacle_screen']])
 line('Drake’s reverse end terminates inside a closed underground shell; applying an exterior approach surface to that end contradicts its locked one-way design. KSNA north-side conflicts are resolved by relocating Page/Powell and the backcountry terraces. **TY2 proposes only the Drake reverse-end exemption; it remains a failure until Ty accepts it.** Any other listed end still needs a layout fix.');line()
 line('Missing: '+ '; '.join(m['ring_missing'])+'. No full clearance/ring pass is claimed for geometry that was never supplied. All of the supplied `ifr` data remains semantically identical to the baseline; Claude owns the final procedure geometry and computed minima.');line()
 title('Height field, landforms, water and continuity')
 line('One standard-library Python authoring evaluator supplies the review grid and both chart/elevation annotations. The grid is 401 × 401, 100 m spacing, little-endian float32 metres MSL, rows south to north, columns west to east. Interpolation uses fixed SW–NE triangle diagonals. Analytic pad planes and cavity decks are detail from the same authoring definition; roofs/arches/bridges become height-aware WorldSolids, not a second ground field. Runtime integration is deferred.');line()
 line('Outer-island contributions fade independently into the ocean and combine by continuous maxima. Pad exterior blends use inverse-distance weights and tend exactly to each plane at its boundary. Finite influence weights fade to zero; only Drake’s named north cliff is intentionally vertical. The ocean continues through the ring with a 19.5–20 km visual fade and no collision wall. Broad arrival/airway cuts are a design prototype for valleys and terraces; they are not final terrain art.');line()
 table(['Peak','Centre E,N km','Top ft MSL','Envelope radius km'],[(q['id'],q['centre'],q['top_ft'],q['radius_km']) for q in w['height_field']['peaks']])
 table(['Crest','Path E,N km','Top ft','Width km'],[(q['id'],q['path'],q['top_ft'],q['width_km']) for q in w['height_field']['crests']])
 table(['Water','Centre E,N km','Surface ft MSL','Radii km'],[(q['id'],q['centre'],q['elevation_ft'],q['radii_km']) for q in w['water']])
 table(['Glacier','Path','Ski-zone centre','Ski-zone ft MSL'],[(q['id'],q['path'],q['ski_zone']['centre'],q['ski_zone']['elevation_ft']) for q in w['glaciers']])
 table(['Canyon','Path','Rim widths m','Floor widths m','Floor ft MSL'],[(q['id'],q['path'],q['rim_width_m'],q['floor_width_m'],q['floor_ft']) for q in w['canyons']])
 title('Airports, runway planes and shore classes')
 line('Each listed runway has 60 m shoulders; exact planes/slopes override the coarse review grid. Coastal ends require ≥0.3 km from the shore; inland fields/airparks/backcountry ends require ≥2 km. The PANC–PALH 0.8 km centre-spacing waiver is the only spacing exception. Eight original airport starts remain; PALH is a PANC float variant and every outer field is a non-start.');line()
 rows=[]
 for a in w['airports']:
  for r in a['runways']:
   ll=r.get('length_m',r.get('length_ft',0)*.3048);ww=r.get('width_m',r.get('width_ft',0)*.3048)
   rows.append([a['id'],r['id'],r['centre'],r['heading_true_deg'],f'{ll:.3f} × {ww:.3f}',a['elevation_ft'],r['surface'],r.get('slope_percent',0),a['shore_class']])
 table(['Field','Magnetic numbers','Centre E,N km','True heading °','Length × width m','ft MSL','Surface','Slope %','Shore class'],rows)
 title('Airparks and retained backcountry strips')
 table(['ID/name','Centre E,N km','True ° / magnetic numbers','Length × width ft','ft MSL','Surface / gear','Slope %','Shore class'],[[q['id']+' '+q['name'],q['centre'],str(q['heading_true_deg'])+' / '+q['numbers_magnetic'],str(q['length_ft'])+' × '+str(q['width_ft']),q['elevation_ft'],q['surface']+'; '+q['gear'],q.get('slope_percent',0),q['shore_class']] for q in w['airparks']])
 line('All 14 retain hangars, houses, windsocks and seeded parked aircraft with the explicit counts/setbacks in the spec. AP8 also has a separate **600 × 120 m water lane at 250 ft**, true 000°, with 60 m shoulders and a 3 m bed offset; it receives the same fit rules as every other strip.');line()
 table(['Strip','Centre E,N km','True heading °','Length × width m','ft MSL','Slope %','Surface','One-way true °'],[[q['id'],q['centre'],q['heading_true_deg'],str(q['length_m'])+' × '+str(q['width_m']),q['elevation_ft'],q['slope_percent'],q['surface'],q.get('one_way_true_deg')] for q in w['backcountry_strips']])
 title('Five outer runway islands, Sitka and navaid sites')
 table(['Island','Airport','Base ft MSL','Coast polygon E,N km'],[[q['id']+' '+q['name'],q['airport'],q['base_ft'],compact(q['coast_polygon'])] for q in w['outer_islands']])
 i=next(i for i in w['outer_islands'] if i.get('volcano'));v=i['volcano'];proof=m['additional_design_checks']['sitka_volcano']
 line('**Sitka Sound** is near Lake Hood on the west perimeter, with twelve tiny surrounding islands and a sheltered east-facing cove whose head reaches the airport fill. SITX is an actual waterfront causeway: water lies 200 m either side of its centreline at the midsection, and broad end lobes preserve the 300 m end setback. The causeway is visible in the chart inset.');line()
 line('The symmetric stratovolcano is centred at '+str(v['centre'])+', radius '+str(v['radius_km'])+' km, with a '+str(v['rim_ft'])+' ft summit rim, '+str(v['crater_floor_ft'])+' ft crater floor and 280 m crater diameter. '+proof['status']+': whole cone disk coast/fade margin '+str(proof['whole_cone_disk_coast_fade_margin_km'])+' km; final-cut margin '+str(proof['whole_cone_final_cut_margin_km'])+' km. Whole-footprint exclusion, rather than radial samples, proves that final/airway cuts do not deform it.');line()
 table(['Site','Position E,N km','ft MSL','Computed ft MSL'],[[q['id'],q['centre'],q['elevation_ft'],next(a['computed_elevation_ft'] for a in m['additional_design_checks']['navaid_sites'] if a['site']==q['id'])] for q in w['outer_navaid_sites']])
 line('These are **sites only**. Claude assigns equipment, idents, frequencies and procedures. Proposed perimeter traffic uses the path '+compact(w['perimeter_traffic_reservation']['path'])+', 350 m flight half-width and full 2 nm terrain screening. Segment MEA targets are '+str(w['perimeter_traffic_reservation']['mea_ft_targets'])+' ft; northern segments rise to 11,000 ft to clear Denali. This proposal does not alter or publish T201.');line()
 title('Landable hard-sand beaches')
 table(['ID/island','Position E,N km','True heading °','Usable length × width m','ft MSL','Slope %','Surface'],[[q['id']+' / '+q['island'],q['centre'],q['heading_true_deg'],str(q['length_m'])+' × '+str(q['width_m']),q['elevation_ft'],q['slope_percent'],q['surface']] for q in w['landable_beaches']])
 line('These are dry upper beach berms with flat cross-sections and explicit usable dimensions, not wet foreshore. They retain 60 m shoulders and ≥300 m shore-end setbacks and receive all field/grade/approach/spacing/ring checks.');line()
 title('Aerobatic boxes and moored markers')
 line('Exactly three IAC boxes remain: two water boxes and only one high-DA box, at McCall. Each is 1,000 m square, true N–S/E–W, with floor 100 m and ceiling 1,100 m above centre ground/water. The judges line is 150 m outside the airport-facing side.');line()
 table(['Box','Centre','DA','Floor–ceiling ft MSL','Nearest full final km','Overhead minimum gap ft'],[[q['id']+' '+q['name'],q['centre'],q['density_altitude'],str(q['floor_msl_ft_target'])+'–'+str(q['ceiling_msl_ft_target']),next(a['nearest_full_final_boundary_km'] for a in m['box_clearances'] if a['box']==q['id']),min(a['clearance_ft'] for b in m['box_clearances'] if b['box']==q['id'] for a in b['overhead_airways'])] for q in w['aerobatic_boxes']])
 for b in w['aerobatic_boxes'][:2]:
  line('**'+b['id']+'**: nine moored marker rafts (one centre cross, four corner Ls, four side Ts), **one additional 12 × 8 m judge raft**, four orange corner buoys; ten rafts total. Cross arms are 40 × 4 m; L/T legs are 30 × 4 m. Every raft is at 0.5 m MSL.');line()
  table(['Raft / shape','Position E,N km'],[[q['id']+' / '+q['shape'],q['centre']] for q in b['rafts']]+[[b['judge_raft']['id']+' / judge',b['judge_raft']['centre']]])
  line('Corner buoys: '+compact([q['centre'] for q in b['corner_buoys']])+'. Dry shore marker: '+compact(b['shore_reference_marker']['centre'])+', on the actual extended judges-line axis. Whole raft and marker bounds are verified in the fit report.');line()
 title('Combat zones, land MOA and airport access')
 line('All zones are **HOT by default**, selectable COLD, with no automatic timed schedule. On entry into the active **3D** HOT volume, that zone’s targets and drones appear; COLD entry produces neither. The active footprint is the polygon union after charted exclusions. Traffic beneath a raised MOA floor does not enter combat airspace. Claude implements those hooks later. Ground targets are fixtures below the aircraft floor; flight/drone volumes remain within the stated floors/ceilings.');line()
 table(['Zone','Reference boundary E,N or sector','Base floor–ceiling ft MSL','Computed floor AGL ft','Computed ceiling AGL ft','Full final / airway minimum km'],[[z['id']+' '+z['name'],compact(z.get('boundary',{'bearings_true_deg':z.get('bearings_true_deg'),'radii_km':z.get('radii_km')})),str(z['floor_msl_ft_target'])+'–'+str(z['ceiling_msl_ft_target']),c['floor_agl_ft_range'],c['ceiling_agl_ft_range'],str(c['minimum_final_boundary_km'])+' / '+str(c['minimum_full_airway_boundary_km'])] for z in w['combat_zones'] for c in m['zone_clearances'] if c['zone']==z['id']])
 line('**CZ5 AP TERN MESA MOA** is a 0.16 km² polygon entirely over Tern Island. Its four vertices, in order, are '+compact(next(z for z in w['combat_zones'] if z['id']=='CZ5')['boundary'])+'. It has **no airport/approach cut-out** and stays at least **2.05 km** from the full known final and airway boundaries, including the proposed perimeter’s full 2 nm terrain swath. It is separate from the airport-over-MOA arrangements.');line()
 table(['MOA / airport','Local MOA floor–ceiling ft MSL','Airport ft / pattern ft','Traffic ceiling ft','Vertical buffer ft','Entire island under active zone'],[[z['zone']+' / '+o['airport'],str(o['floor_msl_ft'])+'–'+str(o['ceiling_msl_ft']),str(next(a['elevation_ft'] for a in w['airports'] if a['id']==o['airport']))+' / '+str(next(a['elevation_ft'] for a in w['airports'] if a['id']==o['airport'])+1000),o['traffic_ceiling_msl_ft'],o['vertical_clearance_ft'],o['entire_island_under_active_zone']] for z in m['zone_clearances'] for o in z['airport_overlays']])
 line('Kite’s whole island and both airport centres lie beneath active combat airspace. Local protection covers complete two-end 4 nm final fans plus 300 m lateral guard and a 1.2 km pattern disk. Arrivals/departures stay at or below 3,000 ft until outside these reservations; combat starts at 5,000 ft, leaving **2,000 ft vertical separation**. No low-floor target, drone orbit or feature flight tube intersects those masks. Outside own-airport vertical reservations, zones have 2.05 km horizontal exclusions around every known final and full airway swath.');line()
 line('The magenta hatch is active airspace; gaps are exclusions, and pale violet shows raised-floor traffic reservations. The thin original sector outline is a chart reference, not permission to engage within a cut-out. Exact active polygon unions are in the fit report. The 100-cell polygonal sector definition is authoritative for this review; radial arc difference is under 0.12 m.');line()
 line('The names are fictional simulator names. Susitna’s real-world name collision was confirmed in the [FAA Alaska chart supplement](https://aeronav.faa.gov/afd/02OCT2025/AK_rear_02OCT2025.pdf); the AP prefix distinguishes this world from real SUA.');line()
 title('Combat terrain, structures, targets and drones')
 for z in w['combat_zones']:
  line('**'+z['id']+' '+z['name']+'**');line()
  table(['Feature','Type / position','Dimensions and clearances'],[[f['id'],f['type']+' / '+compact(f['centre']),compact({k:v for k,v in f.items() if k not in ['id','type','centre']})] for f in z['combat_features']])
  line('Ground targets: '+compact(z['gunnery_targets'])+'. Drone reservation: '+compact(z['drone_orbit'])+'.');line()
 line('Each outer zone has five island/sea-stack landforms with ridges/spires, channels, a 300 m bridge span with 120 m under-clearance and a 100 × 110 m arch opening. CZ5 has a 60 ft dry-canyon floor, 188 ft rims/stacks, 39 m depth, a 120 m bridge span with 100 m under-clearance and a 60 × 55 m arch opening. Island relief, the land canyon and spires are in the common height field. Bridge decks and arch overhangs are analytic WorldSolids design bounds; their openings are not filled by a false terrain roof.');line()
 line('Every complete feature flight tube, target envelope and drone orbit (+20 m aircraft guard) is checked against active polygons, raised floors, analytic terrain maxima and roof clearances. Exact results: `combat_feature_checks` in the fit report.');line()
 title('Caves, Drake and lesson validation')
 line('**Pirate cave** keeps its locked 60 × 26 m leeward mouth and 90 m chamber radius on Catalina. All pad corners lie inside the chamber disk. The 20 m wide entry/chamber chord is 5–23 m MSL above a 3 m flat floor, with ≥6 m throat roof clearance; wreck/driftwood bounds lie outside that strip. The chamber roof is 40 m, authored upper rock at 60 m (full coast-faded chamber bound still gives ≥15 m cover except the intentional skylight). This is a full analytic clearance proof for the stated entry volume and pads, not a claim that a trainer can make an unrestricted airborne U-turn inside the cave.');line()
 line('Pirate proof: `'+compact(m['pirate_cave_verification'])+'`');line()
 line('**Drake** keeps a 1,400 m hill diameter, 320 m rounded relief, 200 m north cliff, 4,700 ft floor and 2,992 ft strip. The strip moved 200 m south so the whole 820 × 420 × 140 m chamber, roof blend and 60 m cover fit inside the hill. DRK remains at (-4.9,-4.3) on the 5,750 ft crown. Exterior length is exactly 500 ft (152.4 m); interior is 759.5616 m, leaving the 60 m end shoulder inside the chamber. Interior deck/shoulders never flatten the upper rock roof.');line()
 line('Drake proof: `'+compact(m['drake_shell_verification'])+'`');line()
 table(['Lesson','Fork / box path','Actual rise m','Required fpm at 80 kt','Required fpm at 50 kt','Loaded ROC upper bound fpm','Result'],[[l['id'],compact(next(q['box_path'] for q in w['lesson_terrain'] if q['id']==l['id'])),l['actual_grid_rise_m'],l['required_fpm_at_80kt'],l['required_fpm_at_50kt'],l['reference_roc_upper_bound_fpm'],l['status']] for l in m['box_canyon_checks']])
 line('Each full piecewise-linear path is tested against the C172-like configuration’s loaded 1,043 kg / 134 kW engine-power ceiling, assuming 100% propeller efficiency, zero drag and no density-altitude power loss. Those deliberately generous assumptions bound sustained climb at every DA. At conservative 50 kt ground speed and 30 m entry clearance, the rising terrain overtakes that path. Runtime trajectories, zoom, turnback, atmospheric lift and collision behavior remain unverified in this docs-only phase.');line()
 title('Hazards, race, legacy features and inventory')
 table(['Tower','Position','Height AGL m','Guy footprint radius m'],[[q['id'],q['centre'],q['height_agl_m'],q['horizontal_envelope_radius_m']] for q in w['hazards']['towers']])
 table(['Wire','Endpoints','Lowest AGL m','Conservative sag fraction'],[[q['id'],q['endpoints'],q['lowest_agl_m'],q['sag_fraction']] for q in w['hazards']['wires']])
 line('All six towers and five wires remain deterministic and charted. Complete guy footprints and conservative full-span wire upper bounds enter clearance checks. T4’s 2,700 ft knoll keeps its 50 m tower top below A2’s 3,000 ft obstruction budget.');line()
 table(['Feature','Position','Design details'],[[q['id']+' '+q['name'],q['centre'],compact({k:v for k,v in q.items() if k not in ['id','name','centre','elements','shell_geometry','interior']})] for q in w['features']])
 line('The race course keeps all 12 original gates/pylons and moves offshore to (10,-13), on moored bases. Whole gate/pylon enclosure final clearance: '+str(m['additional_design_checks']['race']['nearest_full_final_km'])+' km; it is clear of every box and active combat footprint. Carrier stays off OC, clear of the southern LOC BC/hold reservation.');line()
 table(['Inventory ID','Feature/task','Destination','Owner/source'],[[q['id'],q['name'],q['destination'],q.get('owner','')+'; '+q.get('source','')] for q in w['gameplay_inventory']])
 line('The inventory retains all '+str(len(w['gameplay_inventory']))+' original entries: six events, six challenges, lesson/practice variants, rooftop/city, STOL/dusting, tow/float/ski infrastructure, backcountry bars, historic glider slope, carrier, Catalina/Avalon/cave/arch, Powell, glaciers, forest, landable mesas and Drake school geometry. Golden Gate, Eiffel tower, DC Mall and waterfall tunnel remain deleted. No lesson/event/scoring/weather runtime is changed.');line()
 title('Open for Ty — recommended defaults')
 line('A single **approve** can accept the recommended defaults together; it does not start Phase 1B in this session. Locked-decision differences and proposed exceptions remain pending until Ty acts.');line()
 for o in s['open_for_ty']:
  line('**'+o['id']+' — '+o['item']+'**');line();line(o['finding']);line();line('**RECOMMENDED DEFAULT:** '+o['recommended_default']);line();line('Other options: '+'; '.join(o['options'])+'.');line()
 title('Closed review items')
 table(['Item','Resolution'],[[q['item'],q['resolution']] for q in s['closed_for_ty']])
 title('Reproduction and verification')
 line('Run from this worktree, using only Python’s standard library and macOS AppKit:');line();line('```sh\npython3 docs/pending/tools/generate_island.py --png\npython3 docs/pending/tools/verify_island.py --rebuild\n```');line()
 line('Swift/Clang module caches stay in a temporary directory. `island-determinism.json` records byte comparisons and output hashes. The validator checks full-fit recomputation, locked values, untouched IFR, all added zone/field/island/site/beach/raft/cave evidence, XML/PNG dimensions and grid/spec hashes. A successful package check means the reported evidence is consistent; it does not turn FAIL or UNVERIFIED rules into approval.');line()
 line('Review sheets: [map PNG](island-map.png), [map SVG](island-map.svg), [elevation PNG](island-elevation.png), [elevation SVG](island-elevation.svg). The elevation image uses the very same baked grid with the chart annotations; the raw raster is [island-elevation-base.png](island-elevation-base.png). Machine spec: [island-spec.json](island-spec.json).');line()
 title('Complete changes ledger')
 line('Every entry carries item, old value, new value and reason. Baseline 1A entries and chronological partial 1A.2 iterations remain visible; later entries supersede earlier attempts. The final tables above and current `world` object give the final design. This preserves the stopped-session work history rather than pretending earlier candidates were approved.');line()
 for n,c in enumerate(s['changes'],1):
  line('<details>');line('<summary>'+cell(str(n)+'. '+c['item'])+'</summary>');line();line('```json');line(compact(c));line('```');line();line('</details>');line()
